  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the clear best at 0.619 acc, showing that multiprofile + avgpool aggregation is the dominant architectural choice. However, all multimodal experiments so far used concat fusion; we have no evidence on whether weighted fusion could improve the combination of the two modalities. This experiment (config_019) changes only the fusion from concat to weighted while holding every other hyperparameter at the best-known values, making it a clean single-variable test. It clarifies whether the fusion mechanism is a meaningful design lever or a negligible detail. Under a limited budget, resolving this question early is critical: if weighted fusion helps, it becomes the default for all future multimodal experiments (potentially compounding with better image/RNA encoders); if it does not, we can confidently fix concat and redirect remaining budget toward higher-impact dimensions like image encoder (ViT-L) or RNA encoder (scvi/scgpt)."
}

